          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pea protein low FODMAP?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is uncertain. Monash once listed pea protein as low FODMAP at a small serving, but later testing found results varied between brands. Pea protein isolate generally retains fewer oligosaccharides than concentrate. During elimination, choose a certified pea product such as Better Blends, or use egg white or brown rice protein instead."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What ingredients should I avoid in protein powder for IBS?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "On a low FODMAP diet, avoid inulin, chicory root, FOS, the polyols sorbitol, mannitol, xylitol, maltitol and isomalt, honey, agave, apple, pear and mango powders, and whey concentrate or milk powder. Large amounts of mixed gums also bother some people. Unflavored isolates and egg white avoid nearly all of these."
          }
        },
